      "text": "Calculate the probability density function \\(f_{X|Y}(x,0.5)\\) of \\(X\\) given that \\(Y=0.5\\)",
      "solution": "The conditional p.d.f. is \\(f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=\\frac{f_{X,Y}(x,y)}{f_Y(y)}\\) (L6 p.47). Here \\(f_Y(0.5)=\\frac32(1-0.25)=\\frac98\\), and \\(f_{X,Y}(x,0.5)=3x\\) for \\(0.5\\le x\\le1\\), \\(0\\) otherwise. So \\[f_{X|Y}(x,0.5)=\\frac{3x}{9/8}=\\frac{8x}3,\\quad0.5\\le x\\le1,\\] and \\(0\\) otherwise. Check: \\(\\int_{0.5}^1\\frac{8x}3\\,dx=\\frac43(1-0.25)=1\\).",
